  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 88f6fa2b89436164b8e97b17d82dc9a2, type: 3}
  m_Name: 11 - Logical Operators
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: UtilityScriptIWrite::HintSO
  hintId: tutorial_logical_operators
  isUnlockedByDefault: 0
  ignoreLock: 1
  title: Logical Operators
  image: {fileID: 0}
  description: "Logical operators are used to combine or modify Boolean values.\r\nThey
    work with values that are either <font=\"JetBrainsMono SDF\"><color=#55AAFF>True</color></font>
    or <font=\"JetBrainsMono SDF\"><color=#55AAFF>False</color></font>.\r\n\n<font=\"JetBrainsMono
    SDF\"><color=#55AAFF>and</color></font> \u2192 returns <font=\"JetBrainsMono
    SDF\"><color=#55AAFF>True</color></font> if both conditions are <font=\"JetBrainsMono
    SDF\"><color=#55AAFF>True</color></font>\r\n<font=\"JetBrainsMono SDF\"><color=#55AAFF>or
    </color></font> \u2192 returns <font=\"JetBrainsMono SDF\"><color=#55AAFF>True</color></font>
    if at least one condition is <font=\"JetBrainsMono SDF\"><color=#55AAFF>True</color></font>\r\n<font=\"JetBrainsMono
    SDF\"><color=#55AAFF>not</color></font> \u2192 inverts a Boolean value\r\n\nExample:\r\n<font=\"JetBrainsMono
    SDF\">condition = (<color=#55FF55>scan</color>() == <color=#CE9178>\"WhiteOre\"</color>)
    <color=#55AAFF>and</color> (<color=#55FF55>measure</color>() > <color=#B5CEA8>0</color>)</font>\r\n\nThis
    means:\r\n<indent=2em>\u2022 The tile must be <font=\"JetBrainsMono SDF\"><color=#CE9178>\"WhiteOre\"</color></font></indent>\r\n<indent=2em>\u2022
    AND it must have a valid measurable value</indent>\r\n\nResult:\r\nIf both conditions
    are <font=\"JetBrainsMono SDF\"><color=#55AAFF>True</color></font>, then <font=\"JetBrainsMono
    SDF\">condition</font> is <font=\"JetBrainsMono SDF\"><color=#55AAFF>True</color></font>.\r\nOtherwise,
    <font=\"JetBrainsMono SDF\">condition</font> is <font=\"JetBrainsMono SDF\"><color=#55AAFF>False</color></font>."
  isImageBig: 0
